## Changelog Append Policy

- New README Delta entries go to `docs/dev/changelog.md` (backend/system/infra) or `superpatch-frontend/docs/CHANGELOG.md` (frontend).
- Never append deltas to the hub `README.md` or `superpatch-frontend/README.md`; those stay stable references.
- Newest entries go at the top of the changelog files.
- Use the README Delta template below.

## Quick preflight checklist

- Read the root hub, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, and relevant spoke(s)
- Confirm affected stages and data-flow touchpoints
- For schema / migration changes, read existing migrations before writing a new one
- For pathway changes, verify `canonical_ids.json` is the source of truth before editing TS mirrors
- Proceed with TDD and update docs when behavior changes
- Before finalizing, verify doc content matches the implemented code paths

## README Delta template

When recording changes, add a delta block using this structure:

- **What changed**: One-line description of implemented behavior / code change.
- **Why it changed**: One-line rationale (bug fix, feature, refactor, alignment).
- **Code touchpoints**: Paths of changed files (frontend, Edge Functions, Python scripts, pathway JSON).
- **Data-flow impact**: Which stage(s) changed (lead ingest, enrichment, dialer, pathway, webhook-processor, sample, appointment, follow-up, analytics).
- **ID / contract changes**: Pathway / tool / KB / voice / webhook URL changes (or "none"). Link to `canonical_ids.json` if touched.
- **API / schema impact**: Endpoint contract or migration / table / index / RLS changes (or "none").
- **Verification**: Tests / commands / checks performed and result (include `pnpm test` result when frontend code changed).

Append this template to:

- `docs/dev/changelog.md` for backend / system / infra changes
- `superpatch-frontend/docs/CHANGELOG.md` for frontend changes
- `superpatch-frontend/docs/SYSTEM_REVIEW_FINDINGS.md` for cross-cutting integration reviews
